srow(343, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE CAME FROM THE HOLY MYRIADS" — THE MEASURE OF THE HOLY ONE IS NOT THE MEASURE OF FLESH AND BLOOD: FLESH AND BLOOD, MAKING A FEAST FOR HIS SON OR REJOICING AT HIS CANOPY, SHOWS HIS TREASURES AND ALL HE HAS; NOT SO HE WHO SPOKE AND THE WORLD WAS — "FROM THE HOLY MYRIADS", AND NOT ALL THE HOLY MYRIADS. ({SP_(343, 11, "מראה", "הוא", "את", "גנזיו")} "he shows his treasures"; {SP_(343, 11, "ולא", "כל", "רבבות", "קדש")} "and not all the holy myriads"): THE MYRIADS NOT ALL SHOWN — the partitive "from" read strictly (part of the myriads came): the compile\'s parser reads no number here (a construct plural; the ink), the Sifrei\'s reading a quantity of angels unmeasured. The compile: no law. DV33-01. Fresh.')
srow(343, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: A KING OF FLESH AND BLOOD SITS IN HIS PALACE AMONG MEN FAIRER, MORE PRAISED, MIGHTIER THAN HE; NOT SO HE WHO SPOKE AND THE WORLD WAS — "AND HE CAME FROM THE HOLY MYRIADS": HE IS A SIGN (SINGULAR) AMONG THE HOLY MYRIADS, AND WHEN HE WAS REVEALED AT THE SEA THEY KNEW HIM AT ONCE ("THIS IS MY GOD AND I WILL GLORIFY HIM" Exodus 15:2); SO THE NATIONS ASK ISRAEL "WHAT IS YOUR BELOVED MORE THAN ANOTHER BELOVED" (Song of Songs 5:9) THAT YOU DIE FOR HIM ("THEREFORE DO THE MAIDENS LOVE YOU" READ "UNTO DEATH", "FOR YOUR SAKE ARE WE KILLED ALL THE DAY" Psalm 44:23) — COME, MINGLE WITH US; ISRAEL: WE WILL TELL YOU A PART OF HIS PRAISE AND YOU WILL KNOW HIM ("MY BELOVED IS WHITE AND RUDDY …" 5:10-16); THE NATIONS: WE WILL COME WITH YOU ("WHITHER IS YOUR BELOVED GONE" 6:1); ISRAEL: YOU HAVE NO PART IN HIM — "I AM MY BELOVED\'S AND MY BELOVED IS MINE" (6:3). ({SP_(343, 12, "אות", "הוא", "בתוך", "רבבות", "קדש")} "He is a sign among the holy myriads"; {SP_(343, 12, "וכשנגלה", "על", "הים", "מיד", "הכירוהו")} "and when He was revealed at the Sea they knew Him at once"; {SP_(343, 12, "אין", "להם", "חלק", "בו")} "they have no part in Him"): THE SINGULAR ONE — the wordplay "came" (ata) and "sign" (ot); the Sea\'s recognition (Exodus 15:2 on the tape, a RUN CITATION — the song at the Sea\'s compiled span cited); the Song of Songs\' dialogue (the Writings\' seats cited, never read) with the revoweling of "maidens" to "unto death" — the "do not read" move (the song\'s six at sitting 20; the middah of revoweling the compile records by the shelf). The compile: no law — a status on the nations\' exclusion. DV33-01. Fresh.')
srow(343, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM HIS RIGHT HAND A FIERY LAW UNTO THEM" — WHEN THE UTTERANCE WENT OUT FROM THE MOUTH OF THE HOLY ONE IT WENT BY HIS RIGHT TO ISRAEL\'S LEFT, CIRCLED THE CAMP OF ISRAEL TWELVE MIL BY TWELVE MIL, RETURNED BY ISRAEL\'S RIGHT TO HIS LEFT, AND THE HOLY ONE RECEIVED IT IN HIS RIGHT HAND AND ENGRAVED IT ON THE TABLET; ITS VOICE WENT FROM ONE END OF THE WORLD TO THE OTHER ("THE VOICE OF THE LORD HEWS OUT FLAMES OF FIRE" Psalm 29:7). ({SP_(343, 13, "ועוקב", "את", "מחנה", "ישראל", "שנים", "עשר", "מיל")} "and circled the camp of Israel twelve mil"; {SP_(343, 13, "וחוקקו", "בלוח")} "and engraved it on the tablet"): THE UTTERANCE\'S CIRCUIT — the camp twelve mil by twelve mil (the Tosefta\'s measure the song\'s apple of the eye carried at 20b, the same twelve mil — a shelf datum, cited: the compile\'s parameter for the camp\'s size); the tablets engraved by the right hand (Exodus 31:18\'s finger of God, on the tape); the translator sends to the Mekhilta. The compile: the camp\'s twelve mil a parameter already recorded (32:10\'s row). DV33-01. Fresh.')
srow(343, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM HIS RIGHT HAND A FIERY LAW" — IT TELLS THAT THE WORDS OF TORAH ARE LIKENED TO FIRE: AS FIRE WAS GIVEN FROM HEAVEN SO THE WORDS OF TORAH ("YOU HAVE SEEN THAT I SPOKE WITH YOU FROM HEAVEN" Exodus 20:19); AS FIRE IS LIFE TO THE WORLD SO THE WORDS OF TORAH; AS ONE NEAR FIRE IS BURNED AND FAR FROM IT IS COLD, SO THE WORDS OF TORAH — WHILE A MAN LABORS IN THEM THEY ARE LIFE, DEPARTING THEY KILL HIM; AS FIRE SERVES IN THIS WORLD AND THE NEXT SO THE WORDS OF TORAH; AS FIRE MARKS THE BODY OF ITS USER SO THE WORDS OF TORAH; AS FIRE\'S LABORERS ARE KNOWN AMONG MEN, SO THE DISCIPLES OF THE SAGES ARE KNOWN BY THEIR WALK, THEIR SPEECH AND THEIR CLOAK IN THE MARKET. ({SP_(343, 14, "מגיד", "שדברי", "תורה", "משולים", "באש")} "it tells that the words of Torah are likened to fire"; {SP_(343, 14, "נכרים", "בהליכתם", "ובדבורם", "ובעטיפתם", "בשוק")} "known by their walk, their speech and their cloak in the market"): THE SIX LIKENESSES — the qere\'s "fire" and "law" read as one figure (the ketiv one word, Ashdoth\'s — the ink\'s homograph for the compile\'s scan); Exodus 20:19 on the tape (a RUN CITATION); the Tosefta\'s Chagigah 2:6 and Avot de-Rabbi Natan 28 the translator\'s parallels (cited). The compile: no law — a status on the Torah\'s nature. DV33-01. Fresh.')
srow(343, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"A FIERY LAW UNTO THEM" — WERE IT NOT FOR THE LAW GIVEN WITH IT, NO MAN COULD STAND IN IT. ({SP_(343, 15, "אלולא", "דת", "שנתנה", "עמה", "אין", "אדם", "יכול")} "were it not for the law given with it no man could"): THE LAW THAT TEMPERS THE FIRE — the qere\'s second word (dat, the store\'s "royal-edict" gloss — the display patch\'s seat) read as the Torah\'s statutes making the fire bearable: the piska\'s last row, the shortest. The compile: no law. DV33-01. Fresh.')
srow(344, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YEA, HE LOVES THE PEOPLES" (33:3) — IT TEACHES THAT THE PLACE LOVED ISRAEL AS HE LOVED NO NATION OR KINGDOM. ({SP_(344, 1, "מלמד", "שחבב", "המקום", "את", "ישראל")} "it teaches that the Place loved Israel"): THE PEOPLES READ AS ISRAEL — as Onkelos\'s "the tribes" (33:3\'s row); the head row of the piska on 33:3 (the translator\'s twin 97:1, read at chapter 14). The compile: a status on Israel\'s election (7:7-8\'s love on the tape, a RUN CITATION). DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(344, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"ALL HIS HOLY ONES ARE IN YOUR HAND" — THESE ARE THE LEADERS OF ISRAEL WHO GIVE THEIR LIVES FOR ISRAEL: OF MOSES "AND IF NOT, BLOT ME OUT OF YOUR BOOK" (Exodus 32:32); OF DAVID "DID NOT I COMMAND TO NUMBER THE PEOPLE … LET YOUR HAND BE ON ME" (1 Chronicles 21:17). ({SP_(344, 2, "אלו", "פרנסי", "ישראל", "שנותנים", "את", "נפשם", "על")} "these are the leaders of Israel who give their lives for"): THE HOLY ONES THE LEADERS — Moses\' plea at the calf (Exodus 32:32 on the tape, a RUN CITATION) and David\'s at the census plague (the Writings\' seat cited, never read). The compile: no law. DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(344, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SAT DOWN AT YOUR FEET" — THOUGH FORCED, THOUGH BEATEN, THOUGH DESPOILED; "EACH RECEIVING OF YOUR WORDS" — THEY TAKE UPON THEMSELVES AND SAY "ALL THAT THE LORD HAS SPOKEN WE WILL DO AND HEAR" (Exodus 24:7). ({SP_(344, 3, "אף", "על", "פי", "שאנוסים")} "although forced"; {SP_(344, 3, "מקבלים", "עליהם", "ואומרים")} "they take upon themselves and say"): THE ACCEPTANCE UNDER DURESS — Exodus 24:7\'s "we will do and hear" (on the tape, the covenant\'s compiled span cited) read as the sitting at the feet; the row cites no verse of the chapter by marker (its words 33:3\'s). The compile: a status on the covenant\'s acceptance (reference). DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(344, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "YEA, HE LOVES THE PEOPLES" — THE HOLY ONE DID NOT DIVIDE LOVE TO THE NATIONS AS HE DIVIDED IT TO ISRAEL; KNOW IT, FOR THEY SAID: THE ROBBERY OF A FOREIGNER IS PERMITTED AND OF AN ISRAELITE FORBIDDEN; THE KINGDOM SENT TWO OFFICERS: GO, MAKE YOURSELVES JEWS AND SEE WHAT THEIR TORAH IS — THEY WENT TO RABBAN GAMLIEL AT USHA, READ SCRIPTURE, REPEATED THE MISHNAH, MIDRASH (THE EXPOSITION), LAWS AND LORE; AT THEIR LEAVING: ALL THE TORAH IS FINE AND PRAISEWORTHY EXCEPT ONE THING, THAT YOU SAY THE ROBBERY OF A GENTILE IS PERMITTED AND OF AN ISRAELITE FORBIDDEN — AND THIS WE WILL NOT TELL THE KINGDOM. ({SP_(344, 4, "גזלו", "של", "נכרי", "מתר", "ושל", "ישראל", "אסור")} "the robbery of a foreigner permitted and of an Israelite forbidden"; {SP_(344, 4, "ודבר", "זה", "אין", "אנו", "מודיעים", "למלכות")} "and this thing we will not tell the kingdom"): THE TWO SPIES AT USHA — the curriculum named (Scripture, Mishnah, midrash — the exposition, laws, lore: the shelf\'s own vocabulary); THE ROBBERY RULE a Mishnah-grade ruling the spine quotes (Bava Kamma 4:3\'s ox of a gentile the answer sheet\'s neighbor — the compile\'s case, cited; the translator: 16:2-3 rejects it for one standard, read at chapter 1); the officers\' silence. The compile: the robbery rule a DATA row (the code/data law), not a law of the chapter — the blessing\'s "peoples" the hook. DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(344, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"ALL HIS HOLY ONES ARE IN YOUR HAND" — THESE ARE THE GREAT OF ISRAEL WHO ARE HELD IN PLEDGE FOR ISRAEL, AS OF EZEKIEL "LIE ON YOUR LEFT SIDE … I HAVE LAID ON YOU THE YEARS OF THEIR INIQUITY" (Ezekiel 4:4-6). ({SP_(344, 5, "אלו", "גדולי", "ישראל", "שמתמשכנים", "על", "ישראל")} "these are the great of Israel who are pledged for Israel"): THE PLEDGE — Ezekiel\'s bearing of the years (the Prophets\' seat cited, never read); the second reading of "holy ones" (344:2 the leaders, here the great as sureties). The compile: no law. DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(344, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SAT DOWN AT YOUR FEET" — THOUGH THEY PROVOKE, THOUGH THEY SIN; "EACH RECEIVING OF YOUR WORDS" — THEY TAKE ON THEMSELVES THE YOKE OF YOUR TORAH: "ALL THAT THE LORD HAS SPOKEN WE WILL DO AND HEAR". ({SP_(344, 6, "מקבלים", "עליהם", "על", "תורתך")} "they take on themselves the yoke of Your Torah"): THE YOKE — 344:3\'s reading repeated with the sinners in the seat of the oppressed (the same proof, Exodus 24:7). The compile: no law. DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(344, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "YEA, HE LOVES THE PEOPLES" — THE HOLY ONE LOVED ISRAEL AS NO NATION OR KINGDOM; "ALL HIS HOLY ONES ARE IN YOUR HAND" — THESE ARE THE SOULS OF THE RIGHTEOUS LAID IN THE TREASURY ("THE SOUL OF MY LORD SHALL BE BOUND IN THE BUNDLE OF LIFE WITH THE LORD YOUR GOD" 1 Samuel 25:29); "AND THEY SAT DOWN AT YOUR FEET" — EVEN RECOILING TWELVE MIL BACK AND RETURNING TWELVE MIL; "EACH RECEIVING OF YOUR WORDS" — "ALL THAT THE LORD HAS SPOKEN WE WILL DO AND HEAR". ({SP_(344, 7, "אלו", "נפשותיהם", "של", "צדיקים", "שהן", "נתונות", "באוצר")} "these are the souls of the righteous that are laid in the treasury"; {SP_(344, 7, "נרתעים", "לאחוריהם", "שנים", "עשר", "מיל")} "recoiling backward twelve mil"): THE THIRD READING OF THE HOLY ONES — the souls in the treasury (Abigail\'s words, the Prophets\' seat cited, never read; the translator\'s twin in Sifrei Numbers 139), and the twelve mil of the Utterance\'s recoil (343:13\'s circuit, 313:3\'s at chapter 32 — the camp\'s measure, the compile\'s parameter). The compile: a status on the righteous dead (the resurrection\'s doctrine — 33:6\'s rows). DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(345, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"MOSES COMMANDED US A LAW" (33:4) — THIS COMMAND IS ONLY FOR US, ONLY FOR OUR SAKE; SO "I HAVE BUILT THE HOUSE FOR THE NAME OF THE LORD" (1 Kings 8:20) — THE HOUSE FOR WHAT? FOR THE ARK, "AND I HAVE SET THERE A PLACE FOR THE ARK" (8:21): THE COMMAND IS ONLY FOR US. ({SP_(345, 1, "צווי", "זה", "אינו", "אלא", "לנו", "אינו", "אלא")} "this command is only for us, only"; {SP_(345, 1, "בית", "זה", "למה", "לארון")} "this house for what — for the ark"): THE TORAH FOR ISRAEL\'S SAKE as the house for the ark\'s (Solomon\'s words, the Prophets\' seat cited, never read; the ark\'s runner on the tape — 10:1-5 and 31:26 the book beside the ark at 19b). The compile: a status on the Torah\'s addressee. DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(345, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MOSES COMMANDED US A LAW" — DO WE HOLD THE TORAH FROM MOSES? OUR FATHERS EARNED IT: "AN INHERITANCE OF THE CONGREGATION OF JACOB"; I MIGHT HEAR AN INHERITANCE FOR THE SONS OF KINGS — FOR THE SONS OF THE SMALL, WHENCE? "YOU ARE STANDING THIS DAY ALL OF YOU" (29:9); ANOTHER WORD: READ NOT "INHERITANCE" (MORASHAH) BUT "BETROTHED" (ME\'ORASAH) — THE TORAH IS BETROTHED TO ISRAEL AND A MARRIED WOMAN TO THE NATIONS: "CAN A MAN TAKE FIRE IN HIS BOSOM …" (Proverbs 6:27-29). ({SP_(345, 2, "ירשה", "לבני", "קטנים", "מנין")} "an inheritance for the sons of the small, whence"; {SP_(345, 2, "אל", "תהי", "קורא", "מורשה", "אלא", "מאורסה")} "read not \'inheritance\' but \'betrothed\'"): THE INHERITANCE OF ALL AND THE BETROTHAL — 29:9\'s "all of you" the proof for the small (the covenant\'s assembly on the tape; the seat that read this row at chapters 29-31; the outside row 48:9 the same pairing); the "do not read" revoweling (the middah the compile records by the shelf, no count) makes the Torah Israel\'s bride and the nations\' forbidden woman (Proverbs cited, never read). The compile: a status on the Torah\'s ownership (DV33-02), the betrothal a figure. REREAD WHOLE (chapters 29-31\'s reading — 29:9).')
srow(345, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: READ NOT "BETROTHED" BUT "INHERITANCE" — THE TORAH IS AN INHERITANCE TO ISRAEL; A PARABLE OF A KING\'S SON TAKEN CAPTIVE AS A CHILD TO A LAND ACROSS THE SEA: IF HE SEEKS TO RETURN EVEN AFTER A HUNDRED YEARS HE IS NOT ASHAMED, FOR HE SAYS "I RETURN TO MY INHERITANCE" — SO A DISCIPLE OF THE SAGES WHO LEFT THE WORDS OF TORAH FOR OTHER THINGS: EVEN AFTER A HUNDRED YEARS HE IS NOT ASHAMED TO RETURN. ({SP_(345, 3, "מלמד", "שהתורה", "מורשה", "לישראל")} "it teaches that the Torah is an inheritance to Israel"; {SP_(345, 3, "לירשתי", "אני", "חוזר")} "to my inheritance I return"): THE REVOWELING REVERSED — the plain reading restored against 345:2\'s: the inheritance never lapses (the captive prince); the row cites no verse of the chapter by marker (one of the seven), read whole. The compile: no law — a status on the Torah as an estate. DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(346, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE WAS A KING IN JESHURUN" (33:5) — WHEN ISRAEL ARE OF ONE COUNSEL BELOW, HIS GREAT NAME IS PRAISED ABOVE; WHEN? "WHEN THE HEADS OF THE PEOPLE GATHER" — AND GATHERING IS NOTHING BUT THE HEADS OF THE PEOPLE ("TAKE ALL THE HEADS OF THE PEOPLE" Numbers 25:4); ANOTHER WORD: WHEN THE PATRIARCH SEATS THE ELDERS IN THE ACADEMY BELOW HIS NAME IS PRAISED ABOVE — GATHERING IS NOTHING BUT THE ELDERS ("GATHER ME SEVENTY MEN OF THE ELDERS OF ISRAEL" Numbers 11:16). ({SP_(346, 1, "כשישראל", "שוים", "בעצה", "אחת", "מלמטה")} "when Israel are equal in one counsel below"; {SP_(346, 1, "ואין", "אסיפה", "אלא", "זקנים")} "and gathering is nothing but the elders"): THE KING IS THE LORD PRAISED — the head row of 33:5\'s piska: the king in Jeshurun the Name\'s praise when the heads or the elders sit (Numbers 25:4 and 11:16 on the tape — RUN CITATIONS; the Sanhedrin\'s seventy the compiled court\'s parameter); the 20b pointer at 32:15\'s Jeshurun the readback\'s. The compile: a status on the assembly\'s court (reference). DV33-02. Fresh.')
srow(346, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE TRIBES OF ISRAEL TOGETHER" — WHEN THEY ARE ONE BAND AND NOT BANDS AND BANDS ("HE BUILDS HIS UPPER CHAMBERS IN THE HEAVENS AND HIS BAND HE FOUNDED ON THE EARTH" Amos 9:6); R. SHIMON BEN YOCHAI: TWO SHIPS BOUND WITH ANCHORS AND IRON, SET IN THE SEA, A PALACE BUILT ON THEM — BOUND, THE PALACE STANDS; PARTED, IT FALLS; SO WHEN ISRAEL DO HIS WILL HE BUILDS HIS CHAMBERS IN HEAVEN, WHEN NOT, AS IT WERE, HIS BAND IS FOUNDED ON EARTH; SO "THIS IS MY GOD AND I WILL GLORIFY HIM" (Exodus 15:2) — WHEN I ACKNOWLEDGE HIM HE IS GLORIOUS, AND IF NOT, AS IT WERE, IN NAME ALONE; SO "FOR I WILL CALL ON THE NAME OF THE LORD" (32:3) — WHEN I CALL HE IS GREAT; SO "YOU ARE MY WITNESSES AND I AM GOD" (Isaiah 43:12) — WHEN YOU ARE MY WITNESSES I AM GOD, AND IF NOT, AS IT WERE, I AM NOT; SO "TO YOU I LIFT MY EYES, YOU THAT SIT IN THE HEAVENS" (Psalm 123:1) — WERE IT NOT FOR ME, AS IT WERE, YOU WOULD NOT SIT IN THE HEAVENS; AND HERE TOO "THE TRIBES OF ISRAEL TOGETHER" — ONE BAND. ({SP_(346, 2, "כשהם", "עשוים", "אגדה", "אחת")} "when they are made one band"; {SP_(346, 2, "משל", "לאחד", "שהביא", "שתי", "ספינות")} "a parable of one who brought two ships"; {SP_(346, 2, "כשאתם", "עדי", "אני", "אל")} "when you are My witnesses I am God"): THE ONE BAND AND THE FOUR "AS IT WERE" — the two ships (Avot 3:6\'s ten who sit the translator\'s parallel, cited — the compile\'s case), the four verses read conditionally (Exodus 15:2 and 32:3 on the tape as RUN CITATIONS — the row read at chapter 32 for 32:3\'s Name; Isaiah and the psalm cited, never read). The compile: a status on the tribes\' unity (DV33-02), no law. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 32\'s reading — 32:3).')
srow(347, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE TRIBES OF ISRAEL TOGETHER — LET REUBEN LIVE AND NOT DIE" (33:5-6) — WHAT HAS ONE TO DO WITH THE OTHER? A PARABLE OF A KING WHO VISITS HIS SONS AT TIMES; TAKING LEAVE, HIS SONS AND KIN ESCORT HIM: MY SONS, HAVE YOU A NEED, A WORD? — FATHER, WE HAVE NO NEED AND NO WORD, ONLY THAT YOU BE RECONCILED TO OUR ELDEST BROTHER; SO WERE IT NOT FOR THE TRIBES THE PLACE WOULD NOT HAVE BEEN RECONCILED TO REUBEN. ({SP_(347, 1, "וכי", "מה", "ענין", "זה", "לזה")} "and what has this to do with that"; {SP_(347, 1, "אלמלא", "שבטים", "לא", "נתרצה", "המקום", "לראובן")} "were it not for the tribes the Place would not have been reconciled to Reuben"): THE JUXTAPOSITION READ — Reuben\'s blessing follows "together" because the brothers\' plea won him the Place\'s pardon: the piska\'s head row on 33:6 opens with 33:5\'s last words (the seat rule by row: 33:6 the seat, the head). The compile: a status on Reuben\'s pardon (Genesis 35:22 on the tape; 31:6\'s repentance). DV33-03. Fresh.')
srow(347, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"LET REUBEN LIVE AND NOT DIE" — DID HE NOT DIE? WHAT THEN IS "AND NOT DIE"? IN THE WORLD TO COME. ({SP_(347, 2, "והלא", "מת")} "and did he not die"; {SP_(347, 2, "לעולם", "הבא")} "in the world to come"): THE JUSSIVE READ INTO THE WORLD TO COME — Onkelos\'s "eternal life" and "the second death" the same reading in the rendering (33:6\'s row); 329:3 (death and life in one) the outside row\'s. The compile: the resurrection a status (a doctrine row, no law; Sanhedrin 10:1 the answer sheet\'s row, cited — the compile\'s case). DV33-03. Fresh.')
srow(347, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "LET REUBEN LIVE" BY THE DEED OF JOSEPH, "AND NOT DIE" BY THE DEED OF BILHAH; R. CHANANYA BEN GAMLIEL: MERIT IS NEVER EXCHANGED FOR GUILT NOR GUILT FOR MERIT EXCEPT REUBEN\'S AND DAVID\'S ("AND SHIMEI WENT ALONG THE HILLSIDE" 2 Samuel 16:13 … "SOLOMON BUILT THE MILLO" 1 Kings 11:27); THE SAGES: NEVER EXCHANGED — REWARD FOR THE COMMANDMENTS, PUNISHMENT FOR THE TRANSGRESSIONS; THEN WHAT IS "LET REUBEN LIVE AND NOT DIE"? THAT REUBEN REPENTED; RABBAN SHIMON BEN GAMLIEL: REUBEN WAS SAVED FROM THAT SIN AND NEVER CAME TO THAT DEED — COULD HE WHO WOULD STAND AT THE HEAD OF THE TRIBES ON MOUNT EBAL SAYING "CURSED BE HE WHO LIES WITH HIS FATHER\'S WIFE" (27:20) HAVE COME TO THAT DEED? THEN WHAT IS "FOR YOU WENT UP TO YOUR FATHER\'S BED" (Genesis 49:4)? HE AVENGED HIS MOTHER\'S INSULT. ({SP_(347, 3, "לעולם", "אין", "מחליפין", "לא", "זכות", "בחובה")} "merit is never exchanged for guilt"; {SP_(347, 3, "שעשה", "ראובן", "תשובה")} "that Reuben repented"; {SP_(347, 3, "מצל", "היה", "ראובן", "מאותו", "החטא")} "Reuben was saved from that sin"): THREE READINGS OF REUBEN\'S DEED — a dispute in the shelf (R. Chananya ben Gamliel\'s exception, the sages\' rule of no exchange, Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel\'s exoneration by 27:20 — Reuben at Ebal\'s curse the seat that read this row at chapters 26-28; Genesis 49:4 and 35:22 on the tape as RUN CITATIONS; the Babylonian Talmud\'s Shabbat 55b the translator\'s parallel, cited); no rule taken — the ledger\'s two-track note (a DISPUTE row, the reward-and-punishment rule the sages\' the compile holds as a status). DV33-03. REREAD WHOLE (chapters 26-28\'s reading — 27:20).')
srow(347, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND LET HIS MEN BE A NUMBER" — IN THIS WORLD, WHOSE DAYS ARE NUMBERED; BUT IN THE TIME TO COME "LET REUBEN LIVE AND NOT DIE". ({SP_(347, 4, "בעולם", "הזה", "שימיו", "מספר")} "in this world whose days are a number"): THE NUMBER THIS WORLD\'S — the verse\'s two halves two worlds (347:2\'s reading completed); the parser reads no number here (the noun, the ink). The compile: no law. DV33-03. Fresh.')
srow(347, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND LET HIS MEN BE A NUMBER" — MIGHTY IN STRENGTH, MIGHTY IN TORAH: IN STRENGTH, "YOUR MEN SHALL FALL BY THE SWORD AND YOUR MIGHTY IN THE WAR" (Isaiah 3:25); IN TORAH, "MIGHTY IN STRENGTH THAT DO HIS WORD" (Psalm 103:20), AND "BEERAH HIS SON WHOM TILGATH-PILNESER KING OF ASSYRIA CARRIED AWAY, HE WAS PRINCE OF THE REUBENITES" (1 Chronicles 5:6). ({SP_(347, 5, "גבורים", "בכח", "גבורים", "בתורה")} "mighty in strength, mighty in Torah"): THE NUMBERED MEN AS THE MIGHTY — "men" (metim) read by Isaiah\'s "your men" (the Prophets\' and the Writings\' seats cited, never read); Reuben\'s prince in exile the last word of the piska. The compile: no law. DV33-03. Fresh.')
